WEBVTT


WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:01.960
Before we get started,

2
00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.880
be sure you're using a yarn that's
the appropriate weight for your machine.

3
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.520
Just be sure you're using a medium weight

4
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:11.640
yarn that fits in the
hooks of the needles.

5
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:14.400
Do you need yarn on cones
for Machine knitting?

6
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:18.200
No.
All you need is to have the yarn wound

7
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.480
in a way that it will easily
feed into the machine.

8
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.720
Often you can use a center-pull ball

9
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:30.200
from a yarn manufacturer.
Some knitters will use a ball winder

10
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:35.880
and rewind everything, skeins,
hanks balls, everything.

11
00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:39.080
If your ball winder creates a flat bottom

12
00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.520
ball, you can also use the yarn
from the outside of the ball.

13
00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:45.360
Do whatever works for you.

14
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.440
You don't want to spend a whole lot

15
00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.120
of time dealing with knots
as you're knitting.

